-- ownership: items as large as their values in a two-item literal
-- (ownership-v2.md §4.1, #1139's review). An item's fit, its condition
-- reads below the literal's position, its cells and its aggregate are as
-- large as the item: growth chosen before the work, never the item's
-- lane. Each declaration checks, with no lane past its ceiling.
type alias R =
    f0 : List Int
    f1 : List Int
    f2 : List Int
    f3 : List Int
    f4 : List Int
    f5 : List Int
